== Storyline notes ==

* '''KAZUKI controls the block.''' 5-0, 10 points, with Diallo (Round 9, Toyozawa) and the rest of the schedule still to come. The man who ended the 1,095-day reign is running his own table — and the block's only remaining undefeated record belongs to the Shooting Star.
* '''The family's G1 broke in Naruto.''' Taumafa's first loss — a kneebar stoppage, the giant never tapping — came in the same city where Leoni and Vance drew. The Vaiahi family's tournament is now a rebuilding story: the chief drawing, the giant submitted, and Jusuf Muntasir holding the block's most quietly dominant run.
* '''Takagi is the spoiler with a stake.''' 3-2, 6 points, with Taumafa (Round 8, Tsuda) still to come. The Dragon's lariat remains the block's most decisive single move — and the projected Tsuda collision is now a fight to stay in the race at all.
* '''The middle is tightening.''' Kuroki, Ono, and Diallo sit at 4 points — and Ishida, at 6, has joined the chase pack with Jusuf and the Dragon. The rounds ahead will sort the chasers from the passed.

